      <h2>Laser treatment questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="faq-item open"><h4>Is laser hair removal safe long term?</h4><p>Yes — when performed with medical-grade equipment by trained professionals, it's a safe, well-established treatment.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h4>Can you shave in between laser hair removal sessions?</h4><p>Yes, shaving is fine and even recommended between sessions — avoid waxing or plucking instead.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h4>How long should you not shave before laser hair removal?</h4><p>You'll typically be asked to shave within 24 hours of your appointment, not before that.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h4>Is it safe to get laser hair removal while pregnant?</h4><p>We recommend postponing laser treatments during pregnancy — speak with us and your doctor first.</p></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><h4>What happens if you wait too long between sessions?</h4><p>Results may take longer to show since treatment relies on catching hair in its active growth cycle.</p></div>
    </div>
